            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe calls for too much sour cream. I used a little less than 8 ounces, and it was more than enough. I only used about a cup of cheese; I thought the sharp cheddar had an odd taste with the Avocado. I would have chosen Mexican blend or colby jack. I used ghost pepper salsa, but I still needed to add some garlic salt and cumin so that this wasn't too bland.",
            "datePublished": "2023-01-16T04:46:02.888Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AlexandBekahThoughts"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We made this dip for a cinco de mayo party and it really was delicious. At first very bland, but we added a pinch of chili powder, garlic salt, and A LOT of hot sauce! We also decided to heat it up and that worked as well. Personally heated was my favorite.",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-03T19:53:54.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NHBLONDIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious!!! It was one of three new dips at a cookout we went to for the 4th of July and it was the only one that disappeared. Everyone loved it! My final version had a few changes: used 2 cups sharp cheddar cheese, 3 avocadoes, 1 Tablespoon homemade taco seasoning mix. YUM!",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-05T10:02:59.737Z"
          },
          {
